   "text": "I read the molecule as a macrocyclic peptide with three amino acid residues closed through an aryl\u2013thioether\u2013pyrazine linker.\n\n**Residues in the ring**\n- **Ornithine:** its \u03b1-carbon carries a H2N-CH2CH2CH2 side chain, drawn on a wedge. Its \u03b1-NH is bonded to a CH2 on the pyrazine, and its C=O is bonded to the lysine NH.\n- **Lysine:** its \u03b1-carbon carries a (CH2)4NH2 side chain, drawn on a wedge. Its C=O is bonded to the N-methyl nitrogen of the next residue.\n- **N-methyl tryptophan:** its \u03b1-carbon carries a CH2-(indol-3-yl) side chain, drawn on a wedge. Its C=O is bonded to an NH, which is bonded to a CH2 on the benzene ring.\n\n**Linker**\n- **Pyrazine:** the ring is 2,3-disubstituted. One carbon carries the CH2 from the ornithine NH, and the adjacent carbon carries the sulfur.\n- **Benzene:** going round the ring, the carbons carry CH2NH, then S, then Cl, then two CH, then a 4-carboxyphenyl group, which sits next to the CH2NH carbon.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- Working from the wedges, all three \u03b1-carbons come out as S, matching the natural L-amino acids.\n- I converted each to the correct @/@@ in the SMILES by ordering the neighbours as written. This gives @@ for ornithine, @ for lysine and @ for tryptophan.\n\nSMILES: NCCC[C@@H]1NCc2nccnc2Sc2c(CNC(=O)[C@H](Cc3c[nH]c4ccccc34)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](CCCCN)NC1=O)c(-c1ccc(C(=O)O)cc1)ccc2Cl"
